title: Analytics › Process health
route: /analytics
intro: Four small charts and the live workload, in a folded section under 'Detailed breakdowns'. They show whether authorizations are being missed (retro-authorizations), how long a first request takes from referral to approval, how many decisions the payers make each month, and how peer-to-peer calls and appeals ended.
dir: TD
also: The charts follow the payer, program, diagnosis group, site view and period. The live workload card follows the site view, payer and program only, and changes when you answer a payer or accept a denial.
---
start s1 "Under 'Detailed breakdowns', click 'Process health'"
screen sc "Closed: '8% of decisions were retro-authorizations (85). Referral to authorization takes 4.2 days lately.'"
screen a1 "'Retro-authorizations by month'\nColumns of requests made after care began, a sign that an authorization was missed"
screen a2 "'Referral to authorization'\nA line of average days from referral to the payer's decision on first requests"
screen a3 "'Workload: decisions by month'\nStacked columns: approved as requested, approved in part, denied"
screen a4 "'Peer-to-peer calls and appeals'\nBars: the reviewer changed the decision, the decision stood, booked; overturned, partly restored, upheld, no ruling yet"
screen a5 "'Requests on the Dashboard right now'\n'8 handled', '32 still open', a meter\n'Live: it changes when you answer a payer or accept a denial'"
click c1 "Click a month column"
process p1 "Retro-authorizations: opens that month's retrospective requests\nWorkload: opens that month's decisions"
goto g1 "Continues in: Analytics › Case list panel"
input h1 "Hover or Tab to a chart and use the arrow keys"
process h2 "A tooltip with the month's values; the month is read out"
click d1 "Click 'View data table' under a chart"
process d2 "A table of the same numbers"
process p2 "The workload card reads the Dashboard's requests and the site view\nIt is the only part that moves while the demo runs"

s1 --> sc --> a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5
a1 & a3 --> c1 --> p1 --> g1
a1 & a2 & a3 --> h1 --> h2
a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 --> d1 --> d2
a5 --> p2
